  "proof_findings": {
    "different_baseline_adapter": "201 base-only dual vectors are genuinely separate witnesses, not relabelled public YA multipliers; all full 33-variable signed residual boxes are recomputed.",
    "complete_frame_cover": "35 retained witnesses plus five whole-cell closed covers with 17 nonempty cases give 253 payments. All 241 original labels and reflection symmetry are checked; 387 rows, 529 positive multipliers and 288 original PTL entries.",
    "complete_pairs": "All 232324 ordered 482-by-482 combinations are independently tested, leaving exactly 2399 compatible domains; 2342 original witnesses and 57 replacements with 104 closed cases are replayed, with every residual paid.",
    "safe_and_actual_margin": "Safe outer average equals c exactly. Actual frame minimum exceeds ell, so the actual outer margin is (L-ell)/2>0. The minimum low-low pair exceeds c independently.",
    "analytic_transport": "Pair capacity at most two, local mass below sixteen, normalized separated Gram strictly below two, 32 d_epsilon n smoothing, 8c endpoint fee and (51/550)^2>c remain valid. Fix smoothing before the height limit, then take smoothing to zero; all off-line zeros and multiplicities remain in the denominator. Simple and distinct dyadic/cumulative claims are correctly separated from fixed-height numerical counts.",
    "curvature": "The double-Fourier cubic convolution moment is exactly 1/10. The global absolute third derivative bound is <34, and all 256 outward rational point jets plus maximum distance 3/5120 prove w_second>17/100 on the closed interval [9/5,21/10]. This is not consumed by c805460.",
    "active_radical": "For a fixed s,t,a,b the gcd ideal count is bounded by N/(max(q_s q_a^6,q_t q_b^6)); overcounting yields two convergent zeta_K(3) factors. Ten side/exponent choices per active prime and the stated ideal count give N R^(1/2+epsilon). Actual coefficient multiplicity is bounded by d_K(k)^2. The Gram payment uses each restoration tuple own 1/Nprime, preserves nonunit punctures and two heights, and does not supply the unproved large-radical signed cross, global new-target geometry, full count saving or new sigma.",
    "finite_checker_scope": "1349 default checks and 1352 checks with actual source identity are distinct. --certificate compares the finite core, --audit-output writes only an explicit output, default is read-only and -O is rejected. The infinite ideal theorem is the written proof, not a finite-checker output.",
    "publication_status": "README, the current branch queue and notes506 distinguish p506 mathematics from p505 completed formal verification and pending website resource/acceptance work. Previous statements remain historical snapshots."
  },
